Participant: Participant A-01 (synthetic workspace administrator)
Portfolio: Juniper Works / Product Alpha Q3
Interview date: 2026-07-13

Q: When did the product feel useful for the first time?
A: "After I connected one team and saw its work queue, I understood the
promise. Before that, the welcome screen asked me to choose a workflow without
showing what a finished workspace would look like." The participant estimated
the useful moment came after 35-45 minutes of setup and two retries.

Q: What made the retries necessary?
A: The invite step used terms such as owner, manager, and contributor without
showing effective rights. A-01 expected a manager to be able to change a queue
rule; the preview showed read-only access after the invitation was sent.

Q: What would make setup easier for a new admin?
A: A small sample workspace with a visible before/after queue and a checklist:
connect source, invite the first operator, create one rule, review the result.
They preferred clear language over a long guided tour.

Initial codes: time-to-first-value; permissions comprehension; admin automation.
Researcher note: Evidence is detailed for first value and permissions, but this
single account should not set a duration benchmark for all 1,240 synthetic
workspaces.
